{"id":"a1","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":1,"of":16,"title":"Hello, and who you are","titleHe":"שָׁלוֹם","goal":"Greet someone and name yourself and them.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew separates you (m.) from you (f.) — there is no neutral second person. Which one you use depends on who you're speaking to, and you'll be choosing between them in every sentence from here on."},{"type":"table","caption":"Pronouns","head":["","singular","plural"],"rows":[["1st","אֲנִי — I","אֲנַחְנוּ — we"],["2nd m.","אַתָּה — you","אַתֶּם — you"],["2nd f.","אַתְּ — you","אַתֶּן — you"],["3rd m.","הוּא — he","הֵם — they"],["3rd f.","הִיא — she","הֵן — they"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"There is no word for am, is or are. אֲנִי מוֹרֶה is literally I teacher, and means I am a teacher."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"שָׁלוֹם, אֲנִי דָּוִד.","en":"Hello, I'm David."},{"he":"מָה שְׁלוֹמְךָ?","en":"How are you? (to a man)"},{"he":"מָה שְׁלוֹמֵךְ?","en":"How are you? (to a woman)"},{"he":"הִיא מוֹרָה.","en":"She is a teacher."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"שָׁלוֹם","en":"hello, peace","translit":"shalom"},{"he":"תּוֹדָה","en":"thank you","translit":"toda"},{"he":"בְּבַקָּשָׁה","en":"please, you're welcome","translit":"bevakasha"},{"he":"בֹּקֶר טוֹב","en":"good morning","translit":"boker tov"},{"he":"לְהִתְרָאוֹת","en":"see you, goodbye","translit":"lehitra'ot"},{"he":"כֵּן","en":"yes","translit":"ken"},{"he":"לֹא","en":"no, not","translit":"lo"},{"he":"מוֹרֶה","en":"teacher (m.)","translit":"more"},{"he":"מוֹרָה","en":"teacher (f.)","translit":"mora"},{"he":"סְטוּדֶנְט","en":"student (m.)","translit":"student"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["juice","heart","hello, peace","shoes"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שָׁלוֹם","translit":"shalom"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["year","soul, self","dress","thank you"],"correct":3,"prompt":"תּוֹדָה","translit":"toda"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["young","according to","please, you're welcome","café"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בְּבַקָּשָׁה","translit":"bevakasha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["good morning","hat","fire","butter"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֹּקֶר טוֹב","translit":"boker tov"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["light, pale","coat","now","see you, goodbye"],"correct":3,"prompt":"לְהִתְרָאוֹת","translit":"lehitra'ot"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["my, mine","yes","misses, longs for","explains"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כֵּן","translit":"ken"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["no, not","summer","can, is able","goat"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לֹא","translit":"lo"},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___, אֲנִי דָּוִד.","en":"Hello, I'm David.","options":["שָׁלוֹם","לְהִתְרָאוֹת","סְטוּדֶנְט","בֹּקֶר טוֹב"],"correct":0,"full":"שָׁלוֹם, אֲנִי דָּוִד."},{"type":"match","pairs":[["שָׁלוֹם","hello, peace"],["תּוֹדָה","thank you"],["בְּבַקָּשָׁה","please, you're welcome"],["בֹּקֶר טוֹב","good morning"],["לְהִתְרָאוֹת","see you, goodbye"]]},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מוֹרָה","כֵּן","תּוֹדָה","בֹּקֶר טוֹב"],"correct":2,"say":"תּוֹדָה","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “see you, goodbye”?","options":["שֶׁמֶן","מִקְצוֹעַ","לָבוֹא","לְהִתְרָאוֹת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “I am a student”?","options":["אֲנִי סְטוּדֶנְט","אֲנִי הוּא סְטוּדֶנְט","אֲנִי יֵשׁ סְטוּדֶנְט","סְטוּדֶנְט אֲנִי הוּא"],"correct":0,"why":"Hebrew has no word for am — the two words sit side by side."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “thank you”?","options":["סָגֹל","תּוֹדָה","הוֹרִים","קִילוֹ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “teacher (f.)”?","options":["מוֹרָה","אִתִּי","סָלוֹן","יוֹתֵר"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כֵּן","yes"],["לֹא","no, not"],["מוֹרֶה","teacher (m.)"],["מוֹרָה","teacher (f.)"],["סְטוּדֶנְט","student (m.)"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “teacher (f.)” in Hebrew","answer":"מוֹרָה","hint":"mora"}]}